{"name":"Canal Street","hex":"#969281","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Canal Street","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighborhood of Manhattan, New York, New York, United States, centered around the eponymous street.","A neighborhood of Manchester, United Kingdom, centered around the eponymous street along the Rochdale Canal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Canal_Street"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canal Street, Manchester","blocks":[{"text":"Canal Street is a street in Manchester city centre in North West England and the centre of Manchester's gay village. The pedestrianised street, which runs along the west side of the Rochdale Canal, is lined with gay bars and restaurants. The northern end of the street meets Minshull Street and the southern meets Princess Street; part of the street looks across the Rochdale Canal into Sackville Gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Rochdale_Canal_at_Canal_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6953799.jpg/330px-Rochdale_Canal_at_Canal_Street_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6953799.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal_Street%2C_Manchester","wikidata":"Q2935957"},{"title":"Canal Street, Oxford","blocks":[{"text":"Canal Street is a residential street in Jericho, an inner suburb of Oxford, England, northwest of the city centre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Canal_Street_sign_in_Jericho%2C_Oxford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1850504.jpg/330px-Canal_Street_sign_in_Jericho%2C_Oxford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1850504.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal_Street%2C_Oxford","wikidata":"Q15207088"},{"title":"Canal Street (Manhattan)","blocks":[{"text":"Canal Street is a major east–west street in Lower Manhattan, New York City, United States, running over 1 mile (1.6 km) from East Broadway between Essex and Jefferson Streets in the east, to West Street between Watts and Spring Streets in the west. It runs through the neighborhood of Chinatown, and forms the southern boundaries of SoHo and Little Italy as well as the northern boundary of Tribeca. The street acts as a major connector between Jersey City, New Jersey, via the Holland Tunnel (I-78), and Brooklyn in New York City via the Manhattan Bridge. It is a two-way street for most of its length, with two unidirectional stretches between Forsyth Street and the Manhattan Bridge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Canal_St-Baxter_St.JPG/330px-Canal_St-Baxter_St.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal_Street_(Manhattan)","wikidata":"Q1032558"},{"title":"Canal","blocks":[{"text":"Canals or artificial waterways are waterways or engineered channels built for drainage management or for conveyancing water transport vehicles. They carry free, calm surface flow under atmospheric pressure, and can be thought of as artificial rivers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Alter_Strom.jpg/330px-Alter_Strom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal","wikidata":"Q12284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Canal_Street%2C_Manchester.jpg/120px-Canal_Street%2C_Manchester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Canal_Street%2C_Manchester.jpg/250px-Canal_Street%2C_Manchester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Canal_Street%2C_Manchester.jpg/120px-Canal_Street%2C_Manchester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https